      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If a rejoin fixes your microphone then probably re-selecting your microphone could also fix it. (maybe select another microphone and then the one you were using. Even if you have only one microphone you might still have 2 options: the microphone and the same microphone but as default)\n\nMore info:\n\nMost of the times when this happens to me it's right after I lose tracking for my right hand controller. It almost became a reflex. If my right hand loses control for a few seconds I'll double check either in a mirror that my mouth moves as I speak or that the microphone icon lights up as I speak.\n\nWhat I think happens: I own an index. I assume that there's a USB hub of sorts in the headset. So one USB cable goes from the PC to the index headset. Within the headset there is a hub that splits to the \"controller dongles\", microphone, frunk USB port, and speakers. For some reason something happens with this USB hub which disconnects the microphone and the right hand controller. The speaker and left hand seem unaffected.\n\nVRChat seems to handle reconnecting the right hand controller fine however the microphone is quite often not re-enabled / used.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
